<Style id="route"><LineStyle><color>b31b36c4</color><width>3</width></LineStyle></Style>
<Folder><name>01 Tokyo · Nov 28 – Dec 2</name><open>1</open>
<Placemark><name>🏨 Hotel Gracery Shinjuku</name><styleUrl>#sleep</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sleep · 4 nights</b><br/>Godzilla on the roof. Narita Express stops at Shinjuku. Alt: Shibuya Stream Excel.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Hotel+Gracery+Shinjuku&query_place_id=ChIJF-U1JdiMGGARaay7KIrrtZ0'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.702034,35.695358,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Narita Airport (NRT)</name><styleUrl>#transit</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sat Nov 28 · 4:30pm</b><br/>Land. Immigration by 5:30. Buy N&#x27;EX tickets at the counter after customs.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Narita+Airport+(NRT)'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>140.386400,35.764700,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>2. Shibuya Scramble Crossing</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sat Nov 28 · evening</b><br/>Stand in the middle of it. (You go above it tomorrow at sunset.)<br/>≈ 15 min by train from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.695358,139.702034&destination=35.659482,139.700560&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 15 min by train from Gracery · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.695358,139.702034&destination=35.659482,139.700560&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Shibuya+Scramble+Crossing&query_place_id=ChIJK9EM68qLGGARacmu4KJj5SA'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.700560,35.659482,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>3. Senso-ji</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun Nov 29 · 6:30am</b><br/>Tokyo&#x27;s oldest temple at dawn, 30 min, then Nakamise street. By 10am it&#x27;s a mob.<br/>≈ 35 min by metro from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.695358,139.702034&destination=35.714765,139.796655&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 35 min by metro from Gracery · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.695358,139.702034&destination=35.714765,139.796655&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Senso-ji&query_place_id=ChIJ8T1GpMGOGGARDYGSgpooDWw'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.796655,35.714765,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>4. Hatoya Asakusa (matcha)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun Nov 29 · 9am</b><br/>Matcha whisked in front of you. Opens 9; be there at 8:50 or the line is 30 min.<br/>≈ 8 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.714765,139.796655&destination=35.714537,139.801464&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 40 min by metro from Gracery · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.695358,139.702034&destination=35.714537,139.801464&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Hatoya+Asakusa+(matcha)&query_place_id=ChIJnXCWIE2NGGARgRGu9pKd8qM'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.801464,35.714537,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>5. Micasadeco &amp; Cafe (pancakes)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun Nov 29 · 9:45am</b><br/>Ricotta pancakes. Opens 10 on Sunday; the line forms 30 min early. Harajuku.<br/>≈ 40 min by metro from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.714537,139.801464&destination=35.666554,139.705427&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 20 min by metro from Gracery · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.695358,139.702034&destination=35.666554,139.705427&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Micasadeco+&amp;+Cafe+(pancakes)&query_place_id=ChIJDf7Vf6aMGGARzNimzxLN2ds'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.705427,35.666554,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>6. Watchnian Shibuya (pre-owned Rolex etc.)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun Nov 29 · 11:30am</b><br/>Pre-owned Rolex / Omega / Cartier with service records, tax-free, English staff. Dad&#x27;s browse. 5.0 across 1,600 reviews.<br/>≈ 15 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.666554,139.705427&destination=35.659994,139.698840&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 20 min by metro from Gracery · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.695358,139.702034&destination=35.659994,139.698840&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Watchnian+Shibuya+(pre-owned+Rolex+etc.)&query_place_id=ChIJSwFANKiMGGARf4vhiae-dkk'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.698840,35.659994,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>7. Kaiten Sushi Ginza Onodera Honten (Omotesando)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun Nov 29 · 12:30pm</b><br/>Lunch: the high-end conveyor-belt sushi. Chutoro and uni. No reservations; 20–40 min line.<br/>≈ 15 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.659994,139.698840&destination=35.665805,139.710025&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 20 min by metro from Gracery · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.695358,139.702034&destination=35.665805,139.710025&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kaiten+Sushi+Ginza+Onodera+Honten+(Omotesando)&query_place_id=ChIJyZOxItGNGGARWwp9_I4dZDA'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.710025,35.665805,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>8. Solakzade (vintage eyewear)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun Nov 29 · 2pm</b><br/>Opens at 2. Mom&#x27;s frames: vintage stock from the 1800s–1980s, bespoke if she wants, fitted like a tailor. ORDER TODAY: lenses/custom work take about a week. Ship to the Dec 13 hotel (Metropolitan Marunouchi) if not ready. Closed Wed.<br/>≈ 10 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.665805,139.710025&destination=35.668301,139.706347&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 20 min by metro from Gracery · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.695358,139.702034&destination=35.668301,139.706347&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Solakzade+(vintage+eyewear)&query_place_id=ChIJ07gjeKSMGGARXVe4hKptEMA'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.706347,35.668301,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>9. Momotaro Jeans Aoyama</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun Nov 29 · 3pm</b><br/>Selvedge denim. Free hemming, ~1 hr. Pick up after Shibuya Sky (open till 8) or have them send to the hotel.<br/>≈ 12 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.668301,139.706347&destination=35.663737,139.710557&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 20 min by metro from Gracery · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.695358,139.702034&destination=35.663737,139.710557&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Momotaro+Jeans+Aoyama&query_place_id=ChIJLcQt9l-LGGAR0dWhLQOnX-Y'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.710557,35.663737,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>10. MixTHINKS Harajuku (vintage designer bags)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun Nov 29 · 3:30pm</b><br/>Vintage designer bags. Ask the condition grade (N/S/A/AB). Passports for tax-free.<br/>≈ 10 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.663737,139.710557&destination=35.667129,139.703807&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 20 min by metro from Gracery · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.695358,139.702034&destination=35.667129,139.703807&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=MixTHINKS+Harajuku+(vintage+designer+bags)&query_place_id=ChIJd5DukxmNGGAR0dK6sam4DIs'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.703807,35.667129,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>11. Shibuya Sky</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun Nov 29 · 4pm</b><br/>The open-air roof over the crossing. Sunset is 4:28; book the 4pm slot the day tickets open (sunset sells out first). Fuji on a clear day.<br/>≈ 12 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.667129,139.703807&destination=35.658672,139.701985&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 25 min by metro from Gracery · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.695358,139.702034&destination=35.658672,139.701985&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Shibuya+Sky&query_place_id=ChIJ4Rr2JWiLGGARcyRSHuZ-9G8'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.701985,35.658672,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>12. Zauo Shibuya</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun Nov 29 · 6:15pm</b><br/>Fish your own dinner from the boat; they cook it how you want. Reserve. Done by 8.<br/>≈ 8 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.658672,139.701985&destination=35.662474,139.699854&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 20 min by metro from Gracery · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.695358,139.702034&destination=35.662474,139.699854&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Zauo+Shibuya&query_place_id=ChIJa3cs7aiMGGAR8weY287qaJE'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.699854,35.662474,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>13. Tsukiji Outer Market</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Mon Nov 30 · 10am</b><br/>Tsukiji food tour with Ali (ex-Milos seafood chef), 10–noon. Meet at the Shinran Shonin statue. Food not included: bring cash. airbnb.com/experiences/6919404. Not booked yet: book it.<br/>≈ 25 min by metro from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.695358,139.702034&destination=35.664770,139.770252&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 25 min by metro from Gracery · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.695358,139.702034&destination=35.664770,139.770252&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Tsukiji+Outer+Market&query_place_id=ChIJW2cLzSGLGGARXAKXv6EkbqI'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.770252,35.664770,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>14. Kappabashi Kitchen Town</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Mon Nov 30 · 12:30pm</b><br/>Knives engraved with your name. Buy now, forward home in the suitcase.<br/>≈ 20 min by metro from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.664770,139.770252&destination=35.710580,139.787964&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 35 min by metro from Gracery · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.695358,139.702034&destination=35.710580,139.787964&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kappabashi+Kitchen+Town&query_place_id=ChIJXYV-6JWOGGAR85vIZbM1RCE'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.787964,35.710580,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>15. Nishikawa custom pillow (Matsuya Ginza)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Mon Nov 30 · 1:30pm</b><br/>Custom-fit pillow at Nishikawa, Matsuya 7F. Walk-in OK: ~30 min fitting, ~40 min to make, so shop Ginza while it&#x27;s built.<br/>≈ 25 min by metro from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.710580,139.787964&destination=35.672330,139.766762&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 30 min by metro from Gracery · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.695358,139.702034&destination=35.672330,139.766762&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Nishikawa+custom+pillow+(Matsuya+Ginza)&query_place_id=ChIJG8GsGImLGGAR1PfGCC2k-ok'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.766762,35.672330,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>16. Ginza (Uniqlo flagship)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Mon Nov 30 · 2:15pm</b><br/>12-floor Uniqlo, Itoya, depachika food halls. Pick up the pillows on the way out. Passports out for tax-free.<br/>≈ 5 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.672330,139.766762&destination=35.670245,139.763469&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 30 min by metro from Gracery · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.695358,139.702034&destination=35.670245,139.763469&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Ginza+(Uniqlo+flagship)&query_place_id=ChIJb9MHbuaLGGAR0xi-noU25UU'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.763469,35.670245,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>17. teamLab Planets</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Mon Nov 30 · 3:30pm</b><br/>Timed slot. Barefoot, knee-deep in projected koi. Book 3 weeks out.<br/>≈ 15 min by metro from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.670245,139.763469&destination=35.649121,139.789774&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 40 min by metro from Gracery · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.695358,139.702034&destination=35.649121,139.789774&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=teamLab+Planets&query_place_id=ChIJSeco5wiJGGARItbTS8lQ5G0'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.789774,35.649121,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>18. Shimokitazawa (vintage town)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Mon Nov 30 · 5:30pm</b><br/>Shimokitazawa: a whole neighborhood of vintage shops, record stores and cafés. Two hours on foot, no plan.<br/>≈ 50 min by train from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.649121,139.789774&destination=35.660272,139.667263&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 25 min by metro from Gracery · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.695358,139.702034&destination=35.660272,139.667263&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Shimokitazawa+(vintage+town)&query_place_id=ChIJ3dW4JQDzGGARRqcRBSeCqv0'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.667263,35.660272,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>19. T Nakameguro (Omi-beef T-bone)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Mon Nov 30 · 8pm</b><br/>The Tokyo steak: Omi-beef T-bone grilled over an open flame, 4.8 across 500 reviews, one of the top steak rooms in the world. ¥20–30k pp, reservation only (phone 2–5pm JST, or through the hotel). 15 min from Shimokita.<br/>≈ 15 min by train from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.660272,139.667263&destination=35.641193,139.696159&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 30 min by metro from Gracery · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.695358,139.702034&destination=35.641193,139.696159&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=T+Nakameguro+(Omi-beef+T-bone)&query_place_id=ChIJv6eIxzeLGGAR3wUJpK4BB6w'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.696159,35.641193,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>20. Golden Gai</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Mon Nov 30 · 10:45pm</b><br/>Six alleys, 200 six-seat bars, 10 min from the hotel. Start the whisky at Bar Zoetrope. Only if there&#x27;s gas left.<br/>≈ 25 min by train from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.641193,139.696159&destination=35.694112,139.704761&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 5 min by walk from Gracery · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.695358,139.702034&destination=35.694112,139.704761&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Golden+Gai&query_place_id=ChIJr7mGZdmMGGARjxoMFeHApXE'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.704761,35.694112,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Shinjuku Station</name><styleUrl>#transit</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Tue Dec 1 · 7:15am</b><br/>Fuji Excursion train, 7:30 departure. Right side faces the mountain.<br/>≈ 8 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.695358,139.702034&destination=35.689607,139.700571&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 8 min by walk from Gracery · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.695358,139.702034&destination=35.689607,139.700571&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Shinjuku+Station&query_place_id=ChIJH7qx1tCMGGAR1f2s7PGhMhw'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.700571,35.689607,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Kawaguchiko Station</name><styleUrl>#transit</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Tue Dec 1 · 9:20am</b><br/>Arrive lakeside.<br/>≈ 1h50 by train from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.689607,139.700571&destination=35.498236,138.768841&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kawaguchiko+Station&query_place_id=ChIJV3dIuoJgGWAR7bQ0vq8DlE0'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>138.768841,35.498236,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>23. Mt. Tenjo / Fuji Panoramic Ropeway</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Tue Dec 1 · 10am</b><br/>An hour of real climbing to a viewpoint where Fuji fills the horizon. Ropeway down.<br/>≈ 15 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.498236,138.768841&destination=35.503802,138.774378&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Mt.+Tenjo+/+Fuji+Panoramic+Ropeway&query_place_id=ChIJMZmgjCZeGWAR6wB5-jDP5Tk'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>138.774378,35.503802,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>24. Hoto Fudo</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Tue Dec 1 · 12:30pm</b><br/>Hoto: fat-noodle miso stew.<br/>≈ 15 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.503802,138.774378&destination=35.498861,138.768655&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Hoto+Fudo&query_place_id=ChIJD9e0oIJgGWARjCiXDS-GJmA'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>138.768655,35.498861,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>25. Oishi Park</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Tue Dec 1 · 2pm</b><br/>Lakeshore reflection shot.<br/>≈ 25 min by bus from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.498861,138.768655&destination=35.522904,138.745752&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Oishi+Park&query_place_id=ChIJlSsLjKZfGWARBCllOgtTLqI'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>138.745752,35.522904,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>26. Kyubey Ginza</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Tue Dec 1 · 7:30pm</b><br/>Omakase at the classic counter, since 1935. Pack tonight: big bags to the front desk in the morning.<br/>≈ 20 min by metro from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.689607,139.700571&destination=35.668468,139.761270&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 30 min by metro from Gracery · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.695358,139.702034&destination=35.668468,139.761270&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kyubey+Ginza&query_place_id=ChIJu3eG8uiLGGAR14kVvD_YrHI'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.761270,35.668468,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>02 Kanazawa · Dec 2 – 4</name><open>1</open>
<Placemark><name>🏨 Motoyu Ishiya (Fukatani Onsen)</name><styleUrl>#sleep</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sleep · 2 nights</b><br/>Both nights at Motoyu Ishiya, a 200-year-old onsen ryokan in Fukatani, 25 min by taxi from the station (the inn also runs a shuttle: ask). Night 1 with the crab kaiseki in the room; night 2 room + breakfast only, dinner in town. Big bags forwarded Tokyo → Kyoto.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Motoyu+Ishiya+(Fukatani+Onsen)&query_place_id=ChIJYRXlBUMt-F8RB_F70Zzyx74'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>136.720958,36.613703,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tokyo Station</name><styleUrl>#transit</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Wed Dec 2 · 7:45am</b><br/>Hokuriku Shinkansen direct, 8am. Left side for the mountains.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Tokyo+Station&query_place_id=ChIJC3Cf2PuLGGAROO00ukl8JwA'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.767066,35.681300,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Kanazawa Station</name><styleUrl>#transit</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Wed Dec 2 · 10:30am</b><br/>In by 10:30. Overnight bag into a station locker.<br/>≈ 2h30 by train from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.681300,139.767066&destination=36.578044,136.648171&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 35 min by metro from Motoyu Ishiya · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=36.613703,136.720958&destination=36.578044,136.648171&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kanazawa+Station&query_place_id=ChIJBYa7A0Iz-F8R6qe7HgH2XV0'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>136.648171,36.578044,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>3. Iki-iki Tei (Omicho kaisendon counter)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Wed Dec 2 · 11am</b><br/>Omicho Market: the kaisendon counter (write your name on the sheet at the door). Peak snow crab, nodoguro, uni, sweet shrimp. Cash. Closes 1:30.<br/>≈ 15 min by bus from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=36.578044,136.648171&destination=36.571869,136.656385&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 35 min by metro from Motoyu Ishiya · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=36.613703,136.720958&destination=36.571869,136.656385&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Iki-iki+Tei+(Omicho+kaisendon+counter)&query_place_id=ChIJh9CWN3Az-F8RNVCyCT8xvxA'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>136.656385,36.571869,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>4. Kenroku-en</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Wed Dec 2 · 12:30pm</b><br/>Kenroku-en, one of Japan&#x27;s three great gardens. Back in (your new notes call it a must). One hour: the winter yukitsuri rope cones are up on the pines, the pond, the oldest fountain in Japan. Then out.<br/>≈ 15 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=36.571869,136.656385&destination=36.562128,136.662652&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 35 min by metro from Motoyu Ishiya · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=36.613703,136.720958&destination=36.562128,136.662652&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kenroku-en&query_place_id=ChIJBVmy-YMz-F8R5PID8D17Cpc'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>136.662652,36.562128,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>5. Higashi Chaya District</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Wed Dec 2 · 2:15pm</b><br/>1820s teahouse district. Gold-leaf ice cream at Hakuichi, matcha at Amano&#x27;s back room, gild a pair of chopsticks. Two hours of lanes and shops.<br/>≈ 20 min by bus from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=36.562128,136.662652&destination=36.572583,136.666560&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 30 min by metro from Motoyu Ishiya · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=36.613703,136.720958&destination=36.572583,136.666560&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Higashi+Chaya+District&query_place_id=ChIJsfC6oXQz-F8RdA1qXiF6jLs'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>136.666560,36.572583,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>6. Nagamachi Samurai District</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Wed Dec 2 · 4:15pm</b><br/>Earthen walls, narrow lanes.<br/>≈ 20 min by bus from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=36.572583,136.666560&destination=36.563752,136.651015&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 35 min by metro from Motoyu Ishiya · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=36.613703,136.720958&destination=36.563752,136.651015&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Nagamachi+Samurai+District&query_place_id=ChIJhycOJtYz-F8RO54LaTG6_p0'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>136.651015,36.563752,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>7. Nomura-ke Samurai House</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Wed Dec 2 · 4:30pm</b><br/>Real samurai residence: armor, tea room, tiny garden. 45 min, last entry 5.<br/>≈ 3 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=36.563752,136.651015&destination=36.564206,136.650032&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 35 min by metro from Motoyu Ishiya · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=36.613703,136.720958&destination=36.564206,136.650032&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Nomura-ke+Samurai+House&query_place_id=ChIJF_AqPH4z-F8Rmtm1IKiShVQ'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>136.650032,36.564206,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Shirakawa-go Bus Terminal</name><styleUrl>#transit</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Thu Dec 3 · 9:25am</b><br/>Bus drops you at the village gate. Everything walkable.<br/>≈ 1h15 by bus from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=36.578044,136.648171&destination=36.261946,136.906885&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 1h30 by train from Motoyu Ishiya · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=36.613703,136.720958&destination=36.261946,136.906885&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Shirakawa-go+Bus+Terminal&query_place_id=ChIJKx0Jc79x-F8RdUi6Khf_-Is'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>136.906885,36.261946,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>9. Shiroyama Viewpoint</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Thu Dec 3 · 10am</b><br/>The postcard view of 250-year-old gassho farmhouses.<br/>≈ 15 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=36.261946,136.906885&destination=36.263003,136.908558&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 1h30 by train from Motoyu Ishiya · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=36.613703,136.720958&destination=36.263003,136.908558&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Shiroyama+Viewpoint&query_place_id=ChIJ4xHe8r9x-F8RybxsbX5Rr-o'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>136.908558,36.263003,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>10. Wada House</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Thu Dec 3 · 11am</b><br/>Go inside. Hida beef for lunch nearby, then wander the lanes.<br/>≈ 10 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=36.263003,136.908558&destination=36.259905,136.907635&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 1h30 by train from Motoyu Ishiya · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=36.613703,136.720958&destination=36.259905,136.907635&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Wada+House&query_place_id=ChIJdRv_s75x-F8R94Uw560g-iM'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>136.907635,36.259905,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>11. Fukumitsuya Sake Brewery</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Thu Dec 3 · 3pm</b><br/>Sake flight at the 400-year-old brewery.<br/>≈ 15 min by bus from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=36.578044,136.648171&destination=36.553705,136.672340&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 35 min by metro from Motoyu Ishiya · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=36.613703,136.720958&destination=36.553705,136.672340&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Fukumitsuya+Sake+Brewery&query_place_id=ChIJp8mGw4oz-F8RG6DuHOB1z6Y'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>136.672340,36.553705,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>12. Gyohan (jibu-ni duck stew, Korinbo)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Thu Dec 3 · 5:30pm</b><br/>Gyohan, hidden up an alley in Korinbo: jibu-ni (Kanazawa&#x27;s duck stew, Edo-era recipe) and nodoguro grilled with salt; the ¥5,000 local kaiseki set does both. Walk in at 5. Closed Wed; today&#x27;s Thursday.<br/>≈ 15 min by bus from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=36.553705,136.672340&destination=36.564098,136.652682&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 35 min by metro from Motoyu Ishiya · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=36.613703,136.720958&destination=36.564098,136.652682&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Gyohan+(jibu-ni+duck+stew,+Korinbo)&query_place_id=ChIJe96vq38z-F8RebGpcmVcbYQ'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>136.652682,36.564098,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>03 Kyoto · Dec 4 – 9</name><open>1</open>
<Placemark><name>🏨 Hotel Resol Kyoto Kawaramachi Sanjo</name><styleUrl>#sleep</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sleep · 5 nights</b><br/>Central, public bath, Nishiki Market 2 min, Teramachi arcades 1 min, Pontocho out the back. Gion is a 10-min walk. Bags forwarded from Tokyo are waiting here. OPTION for the birthday: move Dec 7–9 to Marufukuro, Tadao Ando&#x27;s hotel inside Nintendo&#x27;s original 1889 headquarters (7 min from Kyoto Station, 20 min from Gion; all-day lounge snacks and drinks, tempura counter; ~$500–700/night).<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Hotel+Resol+Kyoto+Kawaramachi+Sanjo&query_place_id=ChIJq2kbb5MIAWARPjnryqGzDrg'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.769220,35.007950,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Kanazawa Station</name><styleUrl>#transit</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Fri Dec 4 · 9:45am</b><br/>Ryokan taxi/shuttle to the station. 10:15 Thunderbird express along Lake Biwa.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kanazawa+Station&query_place_id=ChIJBYa7A0Iz-F8R6qe7HgH2XV0'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>136.648171,36.578044,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Kyoto Station</name><styleUrl>#transit</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Fri Dec 4 · 12:30pm</b><br/>≈ 2h15 by train from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=36.578044,136.648171&destination=34.985849,135.758767&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 20 min by metro from Hotel Resol · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.007950,135.769220&destination=34.985849,135.758767&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kyoto+Station&query_place_id=ChIJ7wKLka4IAWARCByidG5EGrY'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.758767,34.985849,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>3. Nishiki Market</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Fri Dec 4 · 2pm</b><br/>Kyoto&#x27;s kitchen: five blocks of pickles, tofu doughnuts, knives. Graze for lunch.<br/>≈ 5 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.007950,135.769220&destination=35.005026,135.764723&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 5 min by walk from Hotel Resol · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.007950,135.769220&destination=35.005026,135.764723&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Nishiki+Market&query_place_id=ChIJT8uMzZwIAWARnGzsARCjnrY'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.764723,35.005026,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>4. Teramachi + Shinkyogoku arcades</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Fri Dec 4 · 3:30pm</b><br/>Two covered arcades off the market: vintage, kimono, tea, sneakers. The 2nd-oldest arcade in Japan.<br/>≈ 3 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.005026,135.764723&destination=35.007104,135.767156&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 4 min by walk from Hotel Resol · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.007950,135.769220&destination=35.007104,135.767156&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Teramachi+++Shinkyogoku+arcades&query_place_id=ChIJ6fUyMZQIAWAR4tOOD7AkWJw'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.767156,35.007104,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>5. KUOE Kyoto (build-your-own watch)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Fri Dec 4 · 4:45pm</b><br/>Build-your-own watch at the Kyoto flagship (closed Tue). 2 min from the hotel.<br/>≈ 5 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.007104,135.767156&destination=35.008510,135.766820&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 4 min by walk from Hotel Resol · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.007950,135.769220&destination=35.008510,135.766820&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=KUOE+Kyoto+(build-your-own+watch)&query_place_id=ChIJBc57aw4JAWARNRkUdgsACvY'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.766820,35.008510,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>6. Samurai Kembu Theater</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Fri Dec 4 · 6:30pm</b><br/>90 min: hakama on, learn to draw and cut, then the performance.<br/>≈ 10 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.007950,135.769220&destination=35.009537,135.775539&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 10 min by walk from Hotel Resol · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.007950,135.769220&destination=35.009537,135.775539&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Samurai+Kembu+Theater&query_place_id=ChIJXQxzcPgMAWAR2MVdzqV2kkY'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.775539,35.009537,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>7. Tai Sushi (Kyoto)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Fri Dec 4 · 8:30pm</b><br/>Tai Sushi: shoes off, a family counter, otoro and uni that locals send you to. 5 min from the hotel, 5–10pm, closed Thu/Sun. Reserve or walk in by 8.<br/>≈ 10 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.009537,135.775539&destination=35.004264,135.769804&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 7 min by walk from Hotel Resol · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.007950,135.769220&destination=35.004264,135.769804&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Tai+Sushi+(Kyoto)&query_place_id=ChIJyxIaFZUIAWARMBcBFbbFKCg'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.769804,35.004264,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>8. % Arabica Arashiyama</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sat Dec 5 · 9am</b><br/>% Arabica on the river: the Kyoto latte, opens 9. Be in line at 8:45; by 10:30 it&#x27;s 50 min. Drink it on the riverbank by the bridge.<br/>≈ 35 min by train from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.007950,135.769220&destination=35.013542,135.676437&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 35 min by train from Hotel Resol · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.007950,135.769220&destination=35.013542,135.676437&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=%+Arabica+Arashiyama&query_place_id=ChIJCWDv__-pAWARwLeeqs_cVew'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.676437,35.013542,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>9. Ebisuya rickshaw (Arashiyama)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sat Dec 5 · 9:30am</b><br/>Ebisuya rickshaw, 30 min for two (~¥10,000): they run a rickshaw-only path through the bamboo, no crowds in the photo, and the puller shoots your pictures. 4.9 across 1,700 reviews.<br/>≈ 2 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.013542,135.676437&destination=35.013606,135.677300&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 35 min by metro from Hotel Resol · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.007950,135.769220&destination=35.013606,135.677300&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Ebisuya+rickshaw+(Arashiyama)&query_place_id=ChIJuRmAHACqAWAR9uSfNe-g90s'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.677300,35.013606,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>10. Okochi Sanso Garden</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sat Dec 5 · 10:15am</b><br/>A silent-film star&#x27;s mountain garden, tea included. 45 min, best view in Arashiyama. Then the bamboo on foot if the rickshaw didn&#x27;t cover it.<br/>≈ 8 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.013606,135.677300&destination=35.016715,135.669923&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 40 min by metro from Hotel Resol · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.007950,135.769220&destination=35.016715,135.669923&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Okochi+Sanso+Garden&query_place_id=ChIJGTfQ9gSqAWARvzp3lzOgjk8'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.669923,35.016715,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>11. Steak Otsuka (Arashiyama)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sat Dec 5 · 11:30am</b><br/>Steak Otsuka: the Murasawa sirloin (&#x27;phantom beef&#x27;, 80 head a year) on a hot iron plate, with rice and ponzu. The best wagyu in Kyoto for the money. Opens 11, closed Sun; reserve on TableCheck or be in line at 10:45.<br/>≈ 12 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.016715,135.669923&destination=35.020412,135.680466&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 35 min by metro from Hotel Resol · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.007950,135.769220&destination=35.020412,135.680466&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Steak+Otsuka+(Arashiyama)&query_place_id=ChIJeVvryfipAWARmfvGZx3CApw'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.680466,35.020412,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>12. Sagano Romantic Train (Saga Torokko Sta)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sat Dec 5 · 1pm</b><br/>Sagano Romantic Train one way through the Hozu gorge. Seats open exactly 1 month out (Nov 5): Car No. 5 (open-air), right side. JR back from Umahori.<br/>≈ 10 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.020412,135.680466&destination=35.018568,135.680782&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 35 min by metro from Hotel Resol · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.007950,135.769220&destination=35.018568,135.680782&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Sagano+Romantic+Train+(Saga+Torokko+Sta)&query_place_id=ChIJh2v-m_6pAWAR9TR4D4O6S24'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.680782,35.018568,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>13. Takashimaya Kyoto (Shijo)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sat Dec 5 · 4pm</b><br/>Shijo department-store row: Takashimaya, Daimaru, Fujii Daimaru. Depachika dinner and tax-free on 7F.<br/>≈ 40 min by train from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.018568,135.680782&destination=35.003100,135.768496&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 10 min by walk from Hotel Resol · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.007950,135.769220&destination=35.003100,135.768496&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Takashimaya+Kyoto+(Shijo)&query_place_id=ChIJwzqJepUIAWARvlUYqigZpJI'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.768496,35.003100,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>14. Bar K6</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sat Dec 5 · 8:30pm</b><br/>Japanese whisky nightcap.<br/>≈ 12 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.003100,135.768496&destination=35.013320,135.770556&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 11 min by walk from Hotel Resol · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.007950,135.769220&destination=35.013320,135.770556&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Bar+K6&query_place_id=ChIJ2b4ClM0HAWARHNrgkqv5EDI'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.770556,35.013320,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>15. Kasuga Taisha (Nara)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun Dec 6 · 10:15am</b><br/>45 min to Kintetsu Nara, then the bus up. Start at the top: the lantern-lined cedar path and the vermilion shrine, 30 min. Friendlier deer, no crowds yet.<br/>≈ 1h by train from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.007950,135.769220&destination=34.681545,135.848472&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 1h by train from Hotel Resol · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.007950,135.769220&destination=34.681545,135.848472&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kasuga+Taisha+(Nara)&query_place_id=ChIJ1Wqwa8A5AWARlpXjgoPnl0w'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.848472,34.681545,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>16. Mt. Wakakusa (Nara)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun Dec 6 · 11:15am</b><br/>Mt. Wakakusa: 25 min up a grass hill (¥150) to the view over all of Nara, deer on the slope. Your notes were right: walk DOWN through the park, not up.<br/>≈ 12 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=34.681545,135.848472&destination=34.691150,135.854434&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 1h20 by train from Hotel Resol · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.007950,135.769220&destination=34.691150,135.854434&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Mt.+Wakakusa+(Nara)&query_place_id=ChIJLwbhyrs5AWARXrfL75d3_j8'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.854434,34.691150,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>17. Todai-ji (Nara)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun Dec 6 · 12:30pm</b><br/>Down through the deer park to Todai-ji, the largest wooden building on earth, 50-ft bronze Buddha from 752. Buy the crackers here, where the deer are hungriest. Lunch on Higashimuki shopping street on the way to the train.<br/>≈ 20 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=34.691150,135.854434&destination=34.688985,135.839816&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 1h15 by train from Hotel Resol · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.007950,135.769220&destination=34.688985,135.839816&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Todai-ji+(Nara)&query_place_id=ChIJ3XYIepA5AWARjzzVnT-skPg'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.839816,34.688985,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>18. Fushimi Sake Village</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun Dec 6 · 3pm</b><br/>Willow canal, one counter with 18 breweries.<br/>≈ 45 min by train from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=34.688985,135.839816&destination=34.932500,135.760556&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 35 min by metro from Hotel Resol · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.007950,135.769220&destination=34.932500,135.760556&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Fushimi+Sake+Village&query_place_id=ChIJRwOaco4PAWARzaIhH6-kLG8'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.760556,34.932500,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>19. Fushimi Inari Taisha</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun Dec 6 · 4:30pm</b><br/>10,000 gates. Keep going 30 min past where everyone stops. Open all night.<br/>≈ 15 min by train from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=34.932500,135.760556&destination=34.967695,135.779188&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 25 min by metro from Hotel Resol · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.007950,135.769220&destination=34.967695,135.779188&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Fushimi+Inari+Taisha&query_place_id=ChIJIW0uPRUPAWAR6eI6dRzKGns'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.779188,34.967695,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>20. Taiga Takahashi (T.T)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Mon Dec 7 · 11am</b><br/>Taiga Takahashi: vintage-inspired workwear in a Gion machiya. Then the Hanamikoji / Shijo Gion shops.<br/>≈ 15 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.007950,135.769220&destination=35.001969,135.774332&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 15 min by walk from Hotel Resol · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.007950,135.769220&destination=35.001969,135.774332&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Taiga+Takahashi+(T.T)&query_place_id=ChIJSVB1LIIJAWARSqg5sapwPYo'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.774332,35.001969,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>21. Gion teahouse (tea ceremony, Hanamikoji)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Mon Dec 7 · 12:30pm</b><br/>Lunch in Gion, then the Yasaka backstreets: Ishibe-koji, Nene-no-michi.<br/>≈ 8 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.001969,135.774332&destination=35.003600,135.775000&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 13 min by walk from Hotel Resol · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.007950,135.769220&destination=35.003600,135.775000&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Gion+teahouse+(tea+ceremony,+Hanamikoji)'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.775000,35.003600,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>22. Yasaka Pagoda (Hokan-ji)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Mon Dec 7 · 1:45pm</b><br/>The postcard: the five-story pagoda rising over the stone lane. 10 min, the photo.<br/>≈ 8 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.003600,135.775000&destination=34.998559,135.779178&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 15 min by metro from Hotel Resol · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.007950,135.769220&destination=34.998559,135.779178&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Yasaka+Pagoda+(Hokan-ji)&query_place_id=ChIJIcT4YMUIAWARSTUi4EEky7E'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.779178,34.998559,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>23. Ninenzaka</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Mon Dec 7 · 2pm</b><br/>Stone lanes up the hill. Rent kimono for the walk if Mom&#x27;s in (shops at the bottom of the hill).<br/>≈ 3 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=34.998559,135.779178&destination=34.998399,135.780843&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 15 min by metro from Hotel Resol · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.007950,135.769220&destination=34.998399,135.780843&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Ninenzaka&query_place_id=ChIJlwyrGNAIAWARNb5hUHdZruY'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.780843,34.998399,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>24. Kiyomizu-dera</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Mon Dec 7 · 3:30pm</b><br/>The temple on wooden stilts at golden hour. 45 min, the view is the point.<br/>≈ 10 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=34.998399,135.780843&destination=34.994666,135.784661&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 15 min by metro from Hotel Resol · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.007950,135.769220&destination=34.994666,135.784661&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kiyomizu-dera&query_place_id=ChIJB_vchdMIAWARujTEUIZlr2I'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.784661,34.994666,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>25. Hyotei (3-star kaiseki, since 1837)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Mon Dec 7 · 6pm</b><br/>Hyotei: three stars, 1837, kaiseki in a private garden room. Book through the hotel concierge the day you confirm the trip; it needs a Japanese phone line. Alt: Roan Kikunoi (2*), Gion Nishikawa (2*).<br/>≈ 20 min by taxi from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=34.994666,135.784661&destination=35.011413,135.786762&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 15 min by metro from Hotel Resol · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.007950,135.769220&destination=35.011413,135.786762&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Hyotei+(3-star+kaiseki,+since+1837)&query_place_id=ChIJw5-sbOAIAWAR3IVM2hFyg5A'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.786762,35.011413,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>26. Kikunoi Honten</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Tue Dec 8 · Mom turns 50 · 12:30pm</b><br/>Three-star lunch kaiseki at half the dinner price. The room looks onto a garden in red maple. Two Michelin meals in 24 hours: lunch is the lighter one.<br/>≈ 15 min by taxi from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=34.998559,135.779178&destination=35.001475,135.782056&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 15 min by metro from Hotel Resol · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.007950,135.769220&destination=35.001475,135.782056&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kikunoi+Honten&query_place_id=ChIJVVXF5doIAWARUetIixOU-sw'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.782056,35.001475,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>27. Pontocho Alley</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Tue Dec 8 · Mom turns 50 · 4:30pm</b><br/>The lantern alley at blue hour, a glass of something on the river side.<br/>≈ 15 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.003600,135.775000&destination=35.003934,135.771044&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 9 min by walk from Hotel Resol · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.007950,135.769220&destination=35.003934,135.771044&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Pontocho+Alley&query_place_id=ChIJP2DblBgJAWARAgLlF0vWT6o'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.771044,35.003934,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>28. Yasaka-dori Enraku (private ozashiki)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Tue Dec 8 · Mom turns 50 · 6pm</b><br/>THE DINNER. A private tatami room in a Gion ryotei: kaiseki, open bar, and a maiko AND a geiko with a live shamisen player (the upgrade: base is one maiko with recorded music). Dance, drinking games, conversation through an interpreter, 2–3 hours, cake arranged. ~$1,750 for two with the upgrades, no tipping. Closed Sun; Dec 8 is Tuesday. Request the date now; maiko availability is confirmed close to the day.<br/>≈ 15 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.003934,135.771044&destination=34.998915,135.775630&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 21 min by walk from Hotel Resol · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.007950,135.769220&destination=34.998915,135.775630&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Yasaka-dori+Enraku+(private+ozashiki)&query_place_id=ChIJgfk1fsYIAWAR9JXG1Z1X6uA'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.775630,34.998915,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>04 Osaka · Dec 9 – 11</name><open>1</open>
<Placemark><name>🏨 Cross Hotel Osaka</name><styleUrl>#sleep</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sleep · 2 nights</b><br/>One block from Dotonbori; Amerikamura and Shinsaibashi are a 5-min walk. Alt: Hotel Royal Classic (kabuki-theater building, on Namba Station). Big suitcases forwarded to the Dec 13 Tokyo hotel on the morning of the 11th.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Cross+Hotel+Osaka&query_place_id=ChIJA0zO7hPnAGARHooEfgZ_MsY'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.500763,34.669715,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Kyoto Station</name><styleUrl>#transit</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Wed Dec 9 · 9:30am</b><br/>Shinkansen, 15 min. Bags come with you.<br/>≈ 10 min by metro from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=34.669715,135.500763&destination=34.985849,135.758767&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 10 min by metro from Cross Hotel · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=34.669715,135.500763&destination=34.985849,135.758767&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kyoto+Station&query_place_id=ChIJ7wKLka4IAWARCByidG5EGrY'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.758767,34.985849,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>2. Kuromon Market</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Wed Dec 9 · 11am</b><br/>Kuromon Market: grilled king crab legs, otoro, wagyu skewers, standing up.<br/>≈ 10 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=34.669715,135.500763&destination=34.665351,135.506242&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 10 min by walk from Cross Hotel · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=34.669715,135.500763&destination=34.665351,135.506242&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kuromon+Market&query_place_id=ChIJXSJB5UHnAGARQcEjvngsHaw'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.506242,34.665351,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>3. Sennichimae Doguyasuji (kitchen street)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Wed Dec 9 · 12:30pm</b><br/>150 m of pro kitchen shops: knives, takoyaki pans, the plastic display food. Closes 6pm.<br/>≈ 5 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=34.665351,135.506242&destination=34.664014,135.503506&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 12 min by walk from Cross Hotel · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=34.669715,135.500763&destination=34.664014,135.503506&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Sennichimae+Doguyasuji+(kitchen+street)&query_place_id=ChIJfQfezmvnAGARy4Sd3VGFy_A'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.503506,34.664014,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>4. Shinsaibashi-suji arcade</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Wed Dec 9 · 2pm</b><br/>600 m covered arcade: Uniqlo, drugstores, the giant Don Quijote. Tax-free with passport.<br/>≈ 12 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=34.664014,135.503506&destination=34.672509,135.501366&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 6 min by walk from Cross Hotel · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=34.669715,135.500763&destination=34.672509,135.501366&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Shinsaibashi-suji+arcade&query_place_id=ChIJc7M3_BPnAGARI8OZlTnEXGI'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.501366,34.672509,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>5. B.B. Garage (vintage watches)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Wed Dec 9 · 3:30pm</b><br/>Amerikamura: vintage Americana, and the watch counter at the back. Ask if it&#x27;s been overhauled and if the dial/hands are original. Open till 8, closed Wed → this is Wednesday: swap to Thursday if they&#x27;re closed (see Dec 10).<br/>≈ 8 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=34.672509,135.501366&destination=34.670307,135.498575&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 4 min by walk from Cross Hotel · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=34.669715,135.500763&destination=34.670307,135.498575&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=B.B.+Garage+(vintage+watches)&query_place_id=ChIJ62Sj0EznAGARLILmS20T5LM'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.498575,34.670307,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>6. Dotonbori</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Wed Dec 9 · 5:15pm</b><br/>The canal and the Glico man at dusk. Wanaka takoyaki standing up (one tray, you&#x27;re eating at 7).<br/>≈ 10 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=34.670307,135.498575&destination=34.668647,135.503098&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 4 min by walk from Cross Hotel · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=34.669715,135.500763&destination=34.668647,135.503098&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Dotonbori&query_place_id=ChIJg2DcJhXnAGARCbeAHoZrPeQ'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.503098,34.668647,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>7. Kokuryu Osaka (Kobe-beef kaiseki, Namba 7F)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Wed Dec 9 · 7pm</b><br/>Kokuryu, 7F above Namba: Kobe-beef kaiseki, or the 20-course omakase (bluefin, wagyu, tempura). 4.9 across 1,700 reviews. Reserve.<br/>≈ 8 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=34.668647,135.503098&destination=34.667374,135.501432&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 5 min by walk from Cross Hotel · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=34.669715,135.500763&destination=34.667374,135.501432&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kokuryu+Osaka+(Kobe-beef+kaiseki,+Namba+7F)&query_place_id=ChIJjc46RgDnAGARBnJalgG25Hk'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.501432,34.667374,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>8. Hozenji Yokocho</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Wed Dec 9 · 9:30pm</b><br/>Hozenji Yokocho: the 1-block stone alley behind Dotonbori, lanterns, the moss-covered Buddha you splash with water. 2 min from dinner.<br/>≈ 3 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=34.667374,135.501432&destination=34.668119,135.502610&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 4 min by walk from Cross Hotel · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=34.669715,135.500763&destination=34.668119,135.502610&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Hozenji+Yokocho&query_place_id=ChIJY4ZQxRTnAGAR0mjfWQwO7ho'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.502610,34.668119,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>9. Namba Yasaka Shrine (lion head)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Thu Dec 10 · 8:45am</b><br/>Namba Yasaka: the shrine with a 40-ft lion head for a stage. 20 min, 10 from the hotel, empty this early.<br/>≈ 10 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=34.669715,135.500763&destination=34.661559,135.496704&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 10 min by walk from Cross Hotel · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=34.669715,135.500763&destination=34.661559,135.496704&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Namba+Yasaka+Shrine+(lion+head)&query_place_id=ChIJQVW9eXLnAGARn-pUdRl0w4A'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.496704,34.661559,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>10. Suntory Yamazaki Distillery</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Thu Dec 10 · 10:30am</b><br/>Where Japanese whisky was born. Tour is a lottery 2 months out; tasting counter takes a reservation.<br/>≈ 40 min by train from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=34.661559,135.496704&destination=34.892457,135.674451&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 1h05 by train from Cross Hotel · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=34.669715,135.500763&destination=34.892457,135.674451&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Suntory+Yamazaki+Distillery&query_place_id=ChIJ-WxR9WMDAWARHW0W4OC39qE'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.674451,34.892457,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>11. Grand Front Osaka (Umeda)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Thu Dec 10 · 1:30pm</b><br/>Umeda: Grand Front, Hankyu, the underground mall maze. Lunch on the top-floor restaurant terrace.<br/>≈ 30 min by train from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=34.892457,135.674451&destination=34.703916,135.494010&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 20 min by metro from Cross Hotel · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=34.669715,135.500763&destination=34.703916,135.494010&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Grand+Front+Osaka+(Umeda)&query_place_id=ChIJAQAAB4_mAGAR1alcFGtOaAo'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.494010,34.703916,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>12. Tsutenkaku / Shinsekai</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Thu Dec 10 · 6pm</b><br/>Shinsekai: the 1912 tower, kushikatsu counters, Showa-era signs. Go up for the night view, then take the 60-m spiral slide down (¥1,000). Early night: 7am airport train.<br/>≈ 15 min by metro from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=34.670307,135.498575&destination=34.652499,135.506306&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 15 min by metro from Cross Hotel · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=34.669715,135.500763&destination=34.652499,135.506306&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Tsutenkaku+/+Shinsekai&query_place_id=ChIJ_0Lgd2DnAGARV0X03lbPy-U'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.506306,34.652499,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>05 Seoul · Dec 11 – 13</name><open>1</open>
<Placemark><name>🏨 Andaz Seoul Gangnam</name><styleUrl>#sleep</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sleep · 2 nights</b><br/>Gangnam, where every clinic is. Pool, sauna, hot tub on site for contrast bathing. Direct subway access from B2. Use Naver Map or KakaoMap here; Google Maps can&#x27;t route in Korea.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Andaz+Seoul+Gangnam&query_place_id=ChIJix_5SI6jfDURODDRE4Ama2M'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>127.028920,37.525488,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Namba Station (airport express)</name><styleUrl>#transit</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Fri Dec 11 · 6:50am</b><br/>7am airport express (45 min).<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Namba+Station+(airport+express)'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.502100,34.662700,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Kansai International Airport (KIX)</name><styleUrl>#transit</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Fri Dec 11 · 7:45am</b><br/>Morning flight to Incheon, 2h.<br/>≈ 45 min by train from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=34.662700,135.502100&destination=34.431999,135.236602&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kansai+International+Airport+(KIX)&query_place_id=ChIJ9_rNIxO5AGARiI-QjZ-ncfE'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>135.236602,34.431999,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Incheon International Airport (ICN)</name><styleUrl>#transit</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Fri Dec 11 · 11am</b><br/>Through immigration by noon with the e-Arrival Card. AREX + subway to Gangnam.<br/>≈ 2h by flight from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=34.431999,135.236602&destination=37.458666,126.441968&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 1h45 by train from Andaz · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=37.525488,127.028920&destination=37.458666,126.441968&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Incheon+International+Airport+(ICN)&query_place_id=ChIJWfpeOoOaezUR1L5cy5agS40'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>126.441968,37.458666,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>4. Lucid Dental Clinic (Gangnam)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Fri Dec 11 · 2pm</b><br/>DAD: Lucid Dental, 3–4F, 606 Nonhyeon-ro, 10 min from the hotel. Veneers (&#x27;Lucinate&#x27; laminates): consult, scan, prep and temporaries today (Fri till 6), final seat tomorrow. Send photos on WhatsApp now and confirm two visits is enough. Quoted ₩9.8M (~$7,000) for a full set; not in the budget.<br/>≈ 10 min by taxi from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=37.525488,127.028920&destination=37.507916,127.034088&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 10 min by taxi from Andaz · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=37.525488,127.028920&destination=37.507916,127.034088&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Lucid+Dental+Clinic+(Gangnam)&query_place_id=ChIJv_yR47WjfDURuElu__ohgTM'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>127.034088,37.507916,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>5. AGJ Hana Clinic (NAD+ / glutathione IV)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Fri Dec 11 · 2pm</b><br/>MOM: Hana Clinic, Apgujeong: longevity consult + NAD+ or glutathione IV, 90 min. English, WhatsApp bookings.<br/>≈ 10 min by taxi from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=37.507916,127.034088&destination=37.528293,127.037446&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 15 min by walk from Andaz · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=37.525488,127.028920&destination=37.528293,127.037446&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=AGJ+Hana+Clinic+(NAD++/+glutathione+IV)&query_place_id=ChIJF-_ROQCjfDUR5Miy1Yc2Uq4'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>127.037446,37.528293,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>6. O2ON (hyperbaric oxygen)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Fri Dec 11 · 4pm</b><br/>Hyperbaric oxygen, 60 min. Mom first; Dad joins if the dentist lets him out.<br/>≈ 10 min by taxi from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=37.528293,127.037446&destination=37.520743,127.030209&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 10 min by walk from Andaz · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=37.525488,127.028920&destination=37.520743,127.030209&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=O2ON+(hyperbaric+oxygen)&query_place_id=ChIJu6A69vOjfDURvocQmFQEbFY'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>127.030209,37.520743,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>7. Garosu-gil</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Fri Dec 11 · 5:30pm</b><br/>Tree-lined boutique street, 10 min from the chamber. Olive Young for the K-beauty haul (tax-free with passport).<br/>≈ 10 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=37.520743,127.030209&destination=37.521057,127.022869&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 13 min by walk from Andaz · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=37.525488,127.028920&destination=37.521057,127.022869&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Garosu-gil&query_place_id=ChIJI_IUbOujfDUReyU3t6AyGoM'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>127.022869,37.521057,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>8. SNUH Healthcare System Gangnam Center (38–40F)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sat Dec 12 · 7:30am</b><br/>Both: Seoul National University Hospital&#x27;s Gangnam Center, 38–40F of the Finance Center. The comprehensive checkup: bloods, cardiac CT, abdominal ultrasound, DEXA, sedated endoscopy, plus the brain MRI/MRA add-on. 3–4 hours, English results in a week. Saturday runs till noon. Book NOW (4–6 weeks lead). ~$900–1,500 pp. This is the &#x27;high-tech stuff they&#x27;ve never seen&#x27;.<br/>≈ 10 min by taxi from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=37.525488,127.028920&destination=37.500023,127.036469&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 10 min by taxi from Andaz · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=37.525488,127.028920&destination=37.500023,127.036469&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=SNUH+Healthcare+System+Gangnam+Center+(38–40F)&query_place_id=ChIJu9HgOf6jfDUR0J5KS_pgG_E'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>127.036469,37.500023,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>9. Reberry Clinic Gangnam (skin)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sat Dec 12 · 1:30pm</b><br/>MOM: Reberry: AI skin profiling, then botox (forehead/eyes, 20 min) and the LDM glow, or Thermage if she wants the lift. ~2 hrs. Book 2–4 weeks ahead.<br/>≈ 10 min by taxi from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=37.500023,127.036469&destination=37.501840,127.024645&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 20 min by metro from Andaz · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=37.525488,127.028920&destination=37.501840,127.024645&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Reberry+Clinic+Gangnam+(skin)&query_place_id=ChIJYZZUr5oaO2QRD9IKKBX6Q9U'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>127.024645,37.501840,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>10. Park Jun Beauty Lab Cheongdam (scalp spa)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sat Dec 12 · 4:15pm</b><br/>Both: 15-step scalp spa + neck/back massage in a private room, 90 min. The massage of the trip.<br/>≈ 15 min by taxi from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=37.507916,127.034088&destination=37.518496,127.050210&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 15 min by metro from Andaz · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=37.525488,127.028920&destination=37.518496,127.050210&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Park+Jun+Beauty+Lab+Cheongdam+(scalp+spa)&query_place_id=ChIJsWosT3CkfDURVi3y21bRSUo'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>127.050210,37.518496,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>11. AMORE Seongsu (custom skincare)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sat Dec 12 · 6:30pm</b><br/>Amore Seongsu: AI skin scan and a custom-formulated serum / lipstick. Then Seongsu-dong: warehouses turned cafés, the sneaker shops. Open till 8:30.<br/>≈ 30 min by taxi from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=37.518496,127.050210&destination=37.544410,127.059120&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 20 min by metro from Andaz · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=37.525488,127.028920&destination=37.544410,127.059120&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=AMORE+Seongsu+(custom+skincare)&query_place_id=ChIJsy6u20mlfDURQOlVT0xmv6U'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>127.059120,37.544410,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>12. Inwangsan trailhead</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun Dec 13 · 7:30am</b><br/>Inwangsan: 1.5 hrs up the Seoul fortress wall to the summit at sunrise. Granite, stairs, the whole skyline. Trail shoes.<br/>≈ 35 min by taxi from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=37.525488,127.028920&destination=37.581241,126.954548&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 35 min by taxi from Andaz · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=37.525488,127.028920&destination=37.581241,126.954548&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Inwangsan+trailhead&query_place_id=ChIJwVINcm6jfDURGcu6ZKSQZkY'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>126.954548,37.581241,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>13. Tosokchon Samgyetang</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun Dec 13 · 10am</b><br/>Tosokchon samgyetang: whole ginseng chicken soup, the recovery meal. Opens 10, be in line at 9:50.<br/>≈ 15 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=37.581241,126.954548&destination=37.577779,126.971591&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 35 min by metro from Andaz · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=37.525488,127.028920&destination=37.577779,126.971591&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Tosokchon+Samgyetang&query_place_id=ChIJb5OOGL6ifDURU29ID3t8aOA'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>126.971591,37.577779,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>14. Gyeongbokgung Palace</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun Dec 13 · 11am</b><br/>Rent hanbok by the gate (free palace entry). The photo op of the trip. Non-negotiable. One hour, then out.<br/>≈ 10 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=37.577779,126.971591&destination=37.579617,126.977041&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 35 min by metro from Andaz · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=37.525488,127.028920&destination=37.579617,126.977041&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Gyeongbokgung+Palace&query_place_id=ChIJod7tSseifDUR9hXHLFNGMIs'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>126.977041,37.579617,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>06 Tokyo, last night · Dec 13 – 14</name><open>1</open>
<Placemark><name>🏨 Hotel Metropolitan Tokyo Marunouchi</name><styleUrl>#sleep</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sleep · 1 night</b><br/>On top of Tokyo Station, where the Narita Express leaves from. Suitcases forwarded from Osaka are waiting at the desk; so are Mom&#x27;s frames from Solakzade.<br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Hotel+Metropolitan+Tokyo+Marunouchi&query_place_id=ChIJkwDaxf6LGGARl7WXPY_ic9A'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.768570,35.683897,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Narita Airport (NRT)</name><styleUrl>#transit</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun Dec 13 · 4:30pm</b><br/>Land. Narita Express to Tokyo Station, 1 hour.<br/>≈ 2h30 by flight from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.683897,139.768570&destination=35.764700,140.386400&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 2h30 by flight from Metropolitan · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.683897,139.768570&destination=35.764700,140.386400&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Narita+Airport+(NRT)'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>140.386400,35.764700,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>2. Azabudai Hills</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun Dec 13 · 7pm</b><br/>Azabudai Hills: the rooftop garden / 33F lounge with Tokyo Tower lit up right in front of you (one drink buys the seat). The last photo. 10 min to dinner.<br/>≈ 20 min by taxi from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.683897,139.768570&destination=35.661545,139.740830&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 20 min by taxi from Metropolitan · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.683897,139.768570&destination=35.661545,139.740830&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Azabudai+Hills&query_place_id=ChIJJSI0QC6LGGARwWmKE3MWmj8'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.740830,35.661545,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>3. Sushi Yuu (Nishiazabu)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun Dec 13 · 8pm</b><br/>The second omakase, a tier up. English-speaking chef. Pack it all tonight.<br/>≈ 10 min by taxi from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.661545,139.740830&destination=35.661835,139.725206&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 25 min by metro from Metropolitan · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.683897,139.768570&destination=35.661835,139.725206&travelmode=transit'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Sushi+Yuu+(Nishiazabu)&query_place_id=ChIJ13sWRHqLGGARX9fpN_Tkxfc'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.725206,35.661835,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>4. The Front Room (Marunouchi Bldg)</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Mon Dec 14 · 8:30am</b><br/>The Front Room, Marunouchi Building 1F, 3 min from the hotel: the &#x27;drinkable&#x27; French toast on a hot skillet. Opens 8.<br/>≈ 3 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.683897,139.768570&destination=35.681269,139.763892&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 3 min by walk from Metropolitan · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.683897,139.768570&destination=35.681269,139.763892&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=The+Front+Room+(Marunouchi+Bldg)&query_place_id=ChIJRc0u95GLGGARCt-gXrexQ9Q'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.763892,35.681269,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>5. Imperial Palace East Garden</name><styleUrl>#stop</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Mon Dec 14 · 9:45am</b><br/>Five minutes from the hotel. Check out by noon.<br/>≈ 10 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.681269,139.763892&destination=35.686782,139.757145&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 19 min by walk from Metropolitan · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.683897,139.768570&destination=35.686782,139.757145&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Imperial+Palace+East+Garden&query_place_id=ChIJPfFaQhOMGGAR-QPbNQoAG6M'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.757145,35.686782,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tokyo Station</name><styleUrl>#transit</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<b>Mon Dec 14 · 2:30pm</b><br/>2:45 Narita Express.<br/>≈ 3 min by walk from the previous stop · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.683897,139.768570&destination=35.681300,139.767066&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/>≈ 3 min by walk from Metropolitan · <a href='https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=35.683897,139.768570&destination=35.681300,139.767066&travelmode=walking'>Directions</a><br/><a href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Tokyo+Station&query_place_id=ChIJC3Cf2PuLGGAROO00ukl8JwA'>Open in Google Maps</a>]]></description><Point><coordinates>139.767066,35.681300,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
